(1) Strip `as T`, `!` and `satisfies T` from a handler name before resolving it. A handler that does not resolve to a real function body counts as unresolved, so 2.0 fails. That covers a member, a ref call, and a wrapper arrow whose body only calls something else. The alternative is to follow that call once within the same file.
(2) Resolve the nearest definition BEFORE the listener (searching back from the listener's position), not the first one in the file (:107).
(3) Do not end a statement at a newline that comes right after `=>` (:72).
